WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Our family ran a factory, and people often came to help.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
My mother treated them kindly and often gave them things.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
People wondered, “Why is she so good to them?”

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Then my mother gradually began sharing the gospel with them.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
As the gospel spread, the Spirit worked, and some knelt down to pray.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:51.000
There are many more stories about my mother sharing the gospel.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
One day, a Buddhist nun met my mother on the road.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Mother asked her, “Would you like to go to paradise?”

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.000
She replied, “Yes, I would.”

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Mother told her that those who believe in the Lord have an eternal hope.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
So Mother brought her to hear the gospel.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Mother told her not to be afraid; our God is greater than all.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
She heard the gospel and believed in the Lord.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.000
She broke her vegetarian fast and ate buns and a meat rice dumpling.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
She used to vomit whenever she ate oily food, but that day she did not.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Years later, she was old and seriously ill, and could no longer recognize people.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Mother visited her, and she asked, “Who are you?”

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.000
But she still remembered that she had believed in Jesus.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:12.000
How wonderful! One gospel tract led to the salvation of our whole family.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Later, even my grandfather believed in the Lord.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:27.000
After he believed, Mother said, “Dad, I did not love you enough before.”

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:33.000
“I was not good enough to you or close enough to you. Please forgive me.”

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:41.000
My grandfather was moved and said shyly, “How can you say that?”

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Mother said, “It is so good that I believe in the Lord. I hope you will too.”

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Before long, my grandfather believed too, and our family began meeting together.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.000
That is my mother’s testimony of sharing the gospel.
